From 7c81f9f4f4442cf576a678ae0c1c2f42ccc4307f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 02:54:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] klzh2: four tANS states over two bit streams for chunks
 from 256 symbols, split penalty, branchy loop kept

Decode of the code streams was the cost of the tANS stage: chunks of 256 symbols or more now
use four states over two bit streams; a table more must save 64 (literals) or 32 (codes)
bytes. Mask-based and fully branch-free variants of the sequence loop were measured slower
than the branchy one on this host and are not kept (numbers in results/R01-work/NOTES.md).
The encoder copies short literal runs as 16 bytes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FUEN4aRWhUw7yL7cZMqTmZ
